#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/apps.adoc
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Basic structure"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Modbus device drivers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"xref:edge/implement.adoc[Implementing a Device] walks through a first Modbus "
"device step by step. This page is the reference for tasks, elements and "
"converters. A driver only describes **which registers belong to which "
"Channel**. Connection, scheduling, error handling and conversion are handled "
"by the Modbus Bridge (bundle `+io.openems.edge.bridge.modbus+`). The meter "
"Janitza UMG 96RM-E (`+io.openems.edge.meter.janitza+`, class "
"`+MeterJanitzaUmg96rmeImpl+`) serves as a template here."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bridge and device"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-bridge-and-device
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"The **Bridge** is a separate component: `+Bridge.Modbus.Tcp+` (IP address, "
"port) or `+Bridge.Modbus.Serial+` (RS485). It holds the connection and "
"processes the tasks of all connected devices. Several devices can share a "
"Bridge (e.g. several meters on an RS485 bus)."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-bridge-and-device
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"The **device** inherits from `+AbstractOpenemsModbusComponent+`, implements "
"`+ModbusComponent+` and receives `+modbus_id+` (ID of the Bridge) and "
"`+modbusUnitId+` (Modbus Unit-ID) in the Config."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-bridge-and-device
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"If communication fails, the base class sets the State-Channel "
"`+ModbusCommunicationFailed+` (level WARNING) of the device."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@Designate(ocd = Config.class, factory = true)\n"
"@Component(name = \"Meter.Janitza.UMG96RME\", immediate = true, configurationPolicy = REQUIRE)\n"
"@GenerateTargetsFromReferences(\"Modbus\")\n"
"public class MeterJanitzaUmg96rmeImpl extends AbstractOpenemsModbusComponent\n"
"        implements MeterJanitzaUmg96rme, ElectricityMeter, ModbusComponent, OpenemsComponent, ModbusSlave {\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    @Override\n"
"    @Reference(policy = STATIC, policyOption = GREEDY, cardinality = MANDATORY,\n"
"            target = \"(&(id=${config.modbus_id})(enabled=true))\")\n"
"    protected void setModbus(BridgeModbus modbus) {\n"
"        super.setModbus(modbus);\n"
"    }\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    public MeterJanitzaUmg96rmeImpl() {\n"
"        super(OpenemsComponent.ChannelId.values(),\n"
"              ModbusComponent.ChannelId.values(),\n"
"              ElectricityMeter.ChannelId.values(),\n"
"              MeterJanitzaUmg96rme.ChannelId.values());\n"
"        ElectricityMeter.calculateAverageVoltageFromPhases(this);\n"
"    }\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    @Activate\n"
"    private void activate(ComponentContext context, Config config) throws OpenemsException {\n"
"        this.meterType = config.type();\n"
"        this.invert = config.invert();\n"
"        super.activate(context, config.id(), config.alias(), config.enabled(), config.modbusUnitId());\n"
"    }\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    @Override\n"
"    protected ModbusProtocol defineModbusProtocol() {\n"
"        return new ModbusProtocol(this,\n"
"            new FC3ReadRegistersTask(19000, Priority.HIGH,\n"
"                m(ElectricityMeter.ChannelId.VOLTAGE_L1, new FloatDoublewordElement(19000), SCALE_FACTOR_3),\n"
"                m(ElectricityMeter.ChannelId.VOLTAGE_L2, new FloatDoublewordElement(19002), SCALE_FACTOR_3),\n"
"                m(ElectricityMeter.ChannelId.VOLTAGE_L3, new FloatDoublewordElement(19004), SCALE_FACTOR_3),\n"
"                new DummyRegisterElement(19006, 19011),\n"
"                ...\n"
"                m(ElectricityMeter.ChannelId.ACTIVE_POWER,\n"
"                        new FloatDoublewordElement(19026), INVERT_IF_TRUE(this.invert)),\n"
"                ...));\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"The reference to the Bridge is a **setter method** `+setModbus+`; therefore "
"`+@GenerateTargetsFromReferences+` contains the reference name `+"
"\"Modbus\"+`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"`+super.activate(…, config.modbusUnitId())+` registers the device with the "
"Bridge. The base class creates the protocol once on first access via "
"`+defineModbusProtocol()+` and then keeps it. Values from the Config that "
"influence the protocol (here `+invert+`) must therefore be set **before** "
"`+super.activate+`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"`+ElectricityMeter.calculateAverageVoltageFromPhases(this)+` is an example "
"of calculated Channels: if the device only provides phase values, totals or "
"averages are created via callback."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tasks"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-tasks
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid "A task is a Modbus request over a contiguous register range."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Class\n"
"| Function code\n"
"| Purpose\n"
"\n"
"| `+FC3ReadRegistersTask+`\n"
"| 3\n"
"| read holding registers (most common case)\n"
"| `+FC4ReadInputRegistersTask+`\n"
"| 4\n"
"| read input registers\n"
"| `+FC1ReadCoilsTask+`, `+FC2ReadInputsTask+`\n"
"| 1, 2\n"
"| read coils or digital inputs\n"
"| `+FC6WriteRegisterTask+`\n"
"| 6\n"
"| write one register\n"
"| `+FC16WriteRegistersTask+`\n"
"| 16\n"
"| write several registers\n"
"| `+FC5WriteCoilTask+`\n"
"| 5\n"
"| write one coil\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"The elements of a task must follow each other **without gaps**. Registers "
"that are not needed are filled with `+new DummyRegisterElement(from, to)+`. "
"A read request over a larger range is usually faster than many small ones; "
"some devices, however, limit the number of registers per request or reject "
"ranges with undefined registers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Priority and scheduling"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-priority-and-scheduling
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"The Bridge schedules the tasks per Cycle (`+ModbusWorker+`, "
"`+TasksSupplierImpl+`):"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-priority-and-scheduling
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"**Write tasks** run as early as possible, directly after "
"`+TOPIC_CYCLE_EXECUTE_WRITE+`."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-priority-and-scheduling
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"**Read tasks** run as late as possible so that the values are fresh for "
"`+TOPIC_CYCLE_BEFORE_PROCESS_IMAGE+`."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-priority-and-scheduling
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid "`+Priority.HIGH+`: the read task runs in **every** Cycle."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-priority-and-scheduling
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"`+Priority.LOW+`: per Cycle, **one** LOW task of the whole Bridge runs, in "
"turn. With many LOW tasks, it therefore takes correspondingly many Cycles "
"until a value is renewed. Suitable for meter readings, serial numbers, limit "
"values."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-priority-and-scheduling
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"If the cycle time is not sufficient for all tasks, the Bridge sets the "
"Channel `+CycleTimeIsTooShort+`; `+CycleDelay+` shows the delay."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-priority-and-scheduling
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"A device that repeatedly does not respond is considered defective. Only a "
"single random task is then attempted occasionally so that it does not block "
"the bus for the other devices."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-priority-and-scheduling
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"After how many read errors the values become invalid (`+null+`) is set on "
"the Bridge (“Invalidate elements after how many read Errors?”)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Elements"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Element\n"
"| Registers\n"
"| Type\n"
"\n"
"| `+UnsignedWordElement+`, `+SignedWordElement+`\n"
"| 1\n"
"| 16-bit integer\n"
"| `+UnsignedDoublewordElement+`, `+SignedDoublewordElement+`\n"
"| 2\n"
"| 32-bit integer\n"
"| `+UnsignedQuadruplewordElement+`, `+SignedQuadruplewordElement+`\n"
"| 4\n"
"| 64-bit integer\n"
"| `+FloatDoublewordElement+`, `+FloatQuadruplewordElement+`\n"
"| 2 / 4\n"
"| IEEE-754 float / double\n"
"| `+StringWordElement+`\n"
"| n\n"
"| string\n"
"| `+BitsWordElement+`\n"
"| 1\n"
"| individual bits on Boolean or State-Channels\n"
"| `+CoilElement+`\n"
"| –\n"
"| coil (for FC1/FC5)\n"
"| `+DummyRegisterElement+`\n"
"| n\n"
"| gap, is ignored\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"The word order of multi-part values (`+WordOrder+`) can be set, e.g. "
"`+.wordOrder(WordOrder.LSWMSW)+`, if the device sends the least significant "
"word first."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid "Mapping bits to State-Channels:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"m(new BitsWordElement(32, this)\n"
"        .bit(0, BatteryInverterSinexcel.ChannelId.FAULT_STATUS)\n"
"        .bit(1, BatteryInverterSinexcel.ChannelId.ALERT_STATUS)\n"
"        ...)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Conversion (converter)"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-conversion-converter
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"The third parameter of `+m(channel, element, converter)+` converts register "
"values to Channel values and back when writing "
"(`+ElementToChannelConverter+`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Converter\n"
"| Effect when reading\n"
"\n"
"| `+DIRECT_1_TO_1+` (default)\n"
"| unchanged\n"
"| `+SCALE_FACTOR_1+`, `+_2+`, `+_3+`\n"
"| × 10, × 100, × 1000 (e.g. kV → V or kW → W)\n"
"| `+SCALE_FACTOR_MINUS_1+`, `+_2+`, `+_3+`\n"
"| ÷ 10, ÷ 100, ÷ 1000\n"
"| `+INVERT+`, `+INVERT_IF_TRUE(bool)+`\n"
"| reverse the sign (always or depending on the Config)\n"
"| `+KEEP_POSITIVE+`, `+KEEP_NEGATIVE_AND_INVERT+`\n"
"| only let positive values through, or only negative values and invert them, otherwise 0; useful for distributing a signed power to two Channels\n"
"| `+SET_NULL_FOR_DEFAULT(value)+`\n"
"| adopt an “invalid” value of the device (e.g. 0xFFFF) as `+null+`\n"
"| `+chain(…)+`\n"
"| several converters in a row\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"The unit of the Channel is in its `+Doc+` (e.g. `+Unit.WATT+`). The "
"converter must lead from the device value to exactly this unit. Example: the "
"device provides voltage in V as float, Channel `+VOLTAGE_L1+` is in mV → "
"`+SCALE_FACTOR_3+`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Writing"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"new FC6WriteRegisterTask(135,\n"
"        m(BatteryInverterSinexcel.ChannelId.SET_ACTIVE_POWER, new SignedWordElement(135), SCALE_FACTOR_2))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"The Channel must be a write-channel (`+accessMode+` WRITE_ONLY or "
"READ_WRITE)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"`+setNextWriteValue(v)+` on the Channel immediately passes the value to the "
"element (with conversion via the converter). The write task fetches it in "
"the next write step and **then resets it**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"Consequence: a value is written exactly once. If the device is to receive a "
"setpoint permanently (many inverters require this as a sign of life), the "
"driver must set it anew in every Cycle, typically in `+applyPower()+` or a "
"Cycle Event."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Checking a driver"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-checking-a-driver
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"With `+DummyModbusBridge+`, register contents can be specified in the test "
"and the Channel values checked; see xref:development/testing/component-"
"tests.adoc[Component tests]."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-checking-a-driver
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"On the real Bridge, the setting “Log-Verbosity” shows the Modbus requests in "
"the log."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-checking-a-driver
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/implementing/modbus-device-drivers.adoc
msgid ""
"Via `+ModbusSlave+`/`+getModbusSlaveTable()+`, the driver also provides its "
"Channels in the Modbus/TCP API of the Edge."
msgstr ""
